<BaseLayout title="Editorial & Corrections Policy — VisaPath.pk" description="How VisaPath.pk checks government sources, explains calculator estimates and handles corrections.">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10 prose">
    <h1>Editorial and Corrections Policy</h1>
    <p>Updated 14 November 2026. VisaPath.pk is a Tech Traders publication for Pakistani travellers. Our role is to explain application routes and help readers organise their own research, not to decide eligibility or process applications.</p>
    <h2>Sources and verification</h2>
    <p>For fees, eligibility and legal requirements, we prioritise the responsible government department, embassy or official application service. A fee table should identify its currency, source and verification date. If the current amount cannot be verified, we direct readers to the official quotation rather than supplying a guessed price.</p>
    <p>A review date means the stated content or source was checked on that date. It does not mean a government guarantees the information indefinitely. Where official pages disagree or local missions differ, we explain the limitation and point readers to the responsible office.</p>
    <h2>Original guidance and tools</h2>
    <p>We organise information around practical tasks: selecting the appropriate route, separating fees from optional services, preparing evidence and understanding the difference between visa validity and permitted stay. We do not publish fabricated applicant stories, approval guarantees or unsupported rankings of “easy” embassies.</p>
    <p>Calculators explain their assumptions. Currency conversions are planning estimates, not payment quotes. The Schengen day counter checks the selected 180-day window; it does not establish visa validity, future continuous-stay entitlement or border admission.</p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>Email <a href="mailto:info@visapath.pk">info@visapath.pk</a> with the page URL, the statement in question and a supporting official link if possible. Do not send application documents or identity numbers. We review reports, correct errors and update the page’s review date when substantive changes are made. We cannot answer an individual immigration case on behalf of an authority.</p>
    <h2>Commercial independence</h2>
    <p>Advertisements and any clearly disclosed affiliate arrangements help support the publication. Payment does not determine a government requirement or visa outcome. AdSense approval, ad placement and search ranking are not endorsements of immigration advice.</p>
    <h2>Before you pay or travel</h2>
    <p>Check the linked official service for your nationality, residence, purpose and application date. Your decision letter and border permission take precedence over a general guide. Use a suitably qualified professional for case-specific legal advice.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
